    "narrative": "With the scarcity of stolen bases remaining our primary concern for the home stretch, **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) stands out as our clear offensive anchor today against Dobnak. Batting cleanup in a matchup with a favorable 4.70 xERA, **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a massive 17% boost due to the opposing SP's lack of efficiency, making him our highest-projected start. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (70.36) remains the engine of our lineup; his consistency, paired with a solid 4.22 xERA matchup against Roupp, keeps his floor incredibly high despite a minor platoon disadvantage. **Jonathan Aranda** (67.95) and **Daulton Varsho** (65.74) also command strong starts, with **Jonathan Aranda** leveraging a significant 19% SP skill boost against Bieber and **Daulton Varsho** thriving due to his platoon edge against Grayson Rodriguez.\n\nThe most difficult decision today was balancing the upside of **Zack Gelof** (61.37) against the fringe utility spot held by **Jung Hoo Lee** (44.85). While **Zack Gelof** offers a strong 17% SP skill advantage against Dobnak, **Jung Hoo Lee** is fighting uphill against a 2.99 xERA from Williams; consequently, **Jung Hoo Lee** is relegated to the absolute bottom of our active rotation, barely avoiding the bench. We are tracking \"Lineup Pending\" alerts closely for **Yainer Diaz**, **Cal Raleigh**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Dylan Beavers**, and **Daulton Varsho**, as any deviation from their projected spots could further compress their efficiency scores. While we would love to leverage the speed profiles of **Justin Crawford** or the power of **Bryce Harper**, their inactive status due to off-days forces us to rely on our active core to maintain our statistical lead. Monitor **Dylan Beavers** closely\u2014his matchup against Gerrit Cole carries a 13% penalty that makes him a high-risk, high-reward play despite the park factor helping his outlook.",
